Q02 DeepSeek-flash direct API probes (sanitized)
Date: 2026-09-25
Credential handling: DEEPSEEK_API_KEY was read from the process environment for Authorization headers only. Its value was not printed, logged, or persisted.

Probe A — official OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions
- Endpoint: https://api.deepseek.com/chat/completions
- Model: deepseek-flash
- Request: one short text generation with thinking disabled and max_tokens=16.
- Result: HTTP 200; model deepseek-flash; finish_reason=stop; the requested two-character reply matched.
- Usage: 9 prompt, 1 completion, 10 total tokens.
- Outcome: direct text-generation smoke passed.

Probe B — official Responses API built-in web_search capability
- Endpoint: https://api.deepseek.com/responses
- Model: deepseek-flash
- Request: one short public documentation query with tools=[{"type":"web_search"}] and max_output_tokens=96.
- Result: HTTP 200; response status=incomplete; output contained reasoning only; zero web_search_call items and zero citation annotations.
- Usage: 77 input, 96 output, 173 total tokens.
- Outcome: no real web search occurred. The output cap was reached during reasoning, so this probe does not prove a final answer was delivered. DeepSeek's official Responses API tool table states that built-in web_search is ignored; its Codex setup sets web_search=disabled. Standard API tool calling supports caller-provided functions, which would require an external search implementation and result handoff.

StockQA CLI integration/E2E: not run. No provider adapter was changed. No source documents or company data were requested. No monetary charge receipt was returned by these probes.

Official references checked:
- https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/harness
