- https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/agent_integrations/codex/
- https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/thinking_mode/

Probe C — Anthropic-compatible Messages API with server-side web_search
- Endpoint: https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic/v1/messages
- Model: deepseek-flash
- Request: one public DeepSeek API documentation query using the Anthropic web_search_20250305 tool and max_uses=1.
- Result: HTTP 200; stop_reason=end_turn; content included two server_tool_use blocks and two web_search_tool_result blocks.
- Sources: returned results included https://api-docs.deepseek.com/zh-cn/guides/anthropic_api/ and other DeepSeek docs URLs.
- Usage: 4,808 input, 436 output, 5,244 total tokens; server_tool_use.web_search_requests=2. No currency charge receipt was returned.
- Limit finding: the response reports two server searches although max_uses=1 was requested. Search capability passed; max_uses enforcement did not.
- Outcome: DeepSeek's Anthropic-compatible API can perform server-side web search. The earlier finding that DeepSeek could not search applies only to the OpenAI-compatible Chat/Responses routes tested.

StockQA CLI integration/E2E remains not run. No provider adapter was changed.
